    48	    Theorem A. The Jacobian conjecture in C2 is equivalent to the following
    49	statement:
    50	(∗)   If J(P, Q) ≡ const 6= 0, then the restriction of Q to the curve P = 0
    51	      has only one pole, that is, there is only one irreducible branch at
    52	      infinity of the curve P = 0 such that Q tends to infinity along this
    53	      branch.
    54	   Theorem B. Let f = (P, Q) be a non-zero constant Jacobian polynomial
    55	map of C2 with deg P = kd ≥ deg Q = ke, gcd(d, e) = 1. Then either e = 1
    56	or
    57	                     deggeo f = rd + se ≥ min{2e, d},
    58	where r ≥ 0, s ≥ 0 and r + s ≥ 1.
